commit cfd392e1c0748441241bdfb53b395490eb09b870
Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 21:07:01 2026 -0400

    perf(read): word-at-a-time bit unpack + memset RLE fill

    decodeBitPacked: add a fast path that loads one unaligned u64 per value
    while 8 bytes remain (one bounds check per run, not per value). The
    existing checked loop handles the tail unchanged. RLE runs and the
    trailing zero fill in decode() now use @memset.

    Fix two pre-existing overflows that the new round-trip test (bit widths
    1..31) exposed in the checked/RLE paths: `bit_offset + bit_width + 7` and
    `(bit_width + 7) / 8` were computed in u5 and overflowed for bit_width
    >= 25 (panic in Debug, wrong byte count in ReleaseFast). Both are now
    computed in usize.

    Bench (make bench, ReleaseFast, zig-only, 1M rows, Zig 0.16; clean HEAD
    export vs HEAD + this change, back-to-back, best of 2 runs per cell,
    read_ms / read_rows_per_s):

    | scenario       | before read_ms | after read_ms | before rows/s | after rows/s | delta  |
    |----------------|---------------:|--------------:|--------------:|-------------:|-------:|
    | str_dict       |          76.00 |         66.67 |    13,158,362 |   14,998,283 | +14.0% |
    | int64_nullable |          45.98 |         45.30 |    21,748,303 |   22,076,127 |  +1.5% |

    Other scenarios read (best of 2, before -> after): int64_plain 43.16 -> 43.90,
    f64_plain 42.72 -> 42.60, str_unique 67.59 -> 66.10, mixed5 146.36 -> 143.63.
    Largest regression is int64_plain at +1.7%. file_MB unchanged for every
    scenario (7.63, 7.63, 5.21, 0.84, 13.25, 20.40).

    Tests: 877/877 pass on Zig 0.16 and 0.17 (zig-only), including the new
    round-trip and truncation tests.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
