Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 20:51:34 2026 -0400

    perf(read): adopt first page buffer, skip levels for flat reads

    Single-page chunks now take ownership of the first page's value buffer
    instead of copying it. Def/rep levels are only accumulated when a
    requested column is nested (readRowsFiltered always discards them).

    Bench (zig-only, ReleaseFast, best of 2 runs, read rows/s, pre-2.3 -> 2.3):
      int64_plain     19.87M -> 21.77M  (+10%)
      mixed5           5.33M ->  5.91M  (+11%)
      f64_plain       17.68M -> 23.11M
      int64_nullable  15.84M -> 19.60M
      str_dict        13.25M -> 14.34M
      str_unique      12.47M -> 14.72M
    file_MB unchanged for every scenario.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
