Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 21:03:58 2026 -0400

    perf(read): flat rows for non-nested reads, move instead of clone

    Non-nested reads (and projections with no nested column) now go through
    assembleFlatRows, which moves the decoded cells into the rows instead of
    deep-cloning them. The moved byte payloads already live in the reader's
    bytes arena, so Row.deinit (bytes_borrowed) is unchanged.

    Row gains values_borrowed for producer-owned value blocks (used by the
    iterator arena in the next commit). Only Row.deinit frees row.values.
    Public API addition: Row.values_borrowed (default false).

    Bench (zig-only, ReleaseFast, best of runs, read rows/s, 2.3 -> 2.4):
      mixed5          5.91M -> 8.51M  (+44%)
      str_dict       14.34M -> 19.71M (+37%)
      str_unique     14.72M -> 20.12M (+37%)
      int64_plain    21.77M -> 26.67M (+22%)
      f64_plain      23.11M -> 27.99M (+21%)
      int64_nullable 19.60M -> 25.32M (+29%)
    file_MB unchanged for every scenario.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
